          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "بیٹا (beṭā) is a tadbhava, a word inherited and reshaped by sound change. It comes from beṭṭa, \"boy\", a form CDIAL reconstructs from its descendants (CDIAL 9238). CDIAL lists it in an entry headed biḍḍa, \"defective\", beside Prakrit biṭṭa, \"boy\"; no Sanskrit source is agreed."
            }
          ]
        },
